import PolicyLayout from '../../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Privacy Notice"
  description="What personal information STEM+C collects about participants and families, why, how long it is kept, and who can see it."
  effective="the 2026–2027 season"
  noticeTitle="Draft — pending legal review"
  notice="This notice describes our intended practices and has not yet been reviewed by counsel. It should be reviewed alongside the consent agreement before registration opens."
  noticeTone="warning"
  pdf="/policies/stemplusc-privacy-notice.pdf"
>
  <p>
    This notice explains what personal information STEM+C collects about students and families, why
    we collect it, how long we keep it, and who can see it. It covers our robotics programs — Tie
    Dye Samurai and Tie Dye Jedi — and this website.
  </p>
  <p>
    We are a small, volunteer-run nonprofit. We collect what we need to run a safe program and reach
    someone in an emergency, and not more than that.
  </p>

  <h2>Registration is completed by a parent or guardian</h2>
  <p>
    For any participant under 18, registration is completed by a parent or legal guardian — not by
    the student. The parent provides the student's information as part of their own signing session.
    We do not ask students to submit their personal information to us online.
  </p>
  <p>
    This matters most for our younger participants. Tie Dye Jedi serves grades 6&ndash;9, and some
    participants are under 13. Directing collection through the parent is deliberate.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Student:</strong> name and grade. Email and phone are optional and we encourage
      families of younger students to leave them blank. <strong>We do not ask for a date of
      birth.</strong>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Parents and guardians:</strong> name, email, phone, and relationship to the student,
      for at least one and optionally a second.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Health and emergency information:</strong> allergies, medical conditions, activity
      restrictions, and medications our mentors would need to know about in an emergency.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your media choice:</strong> whether we may use photographs and video of the student.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Signature records:</strong> the executed agreements, who signed, in what capacity, and
      when.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Payment records:</strong> handled by our payment processor. We see that dues were paid
      and by whom; we do not receive or store card numbers or bank details.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not collect Social Security numbers, government ID numbers, immigration status, or school
    records.
  </p>

  <h2>What this website collects</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Nothing about participants.</strong> This site is a set of static pages. Registration
    happens on a separate secure signing platform, and payments on a separate payment platform.
  </p>
  <p>
    The one exception is our contact form, which sends us the name, email, and message you choose to
    type into it. Our web host keeps ordinary server logs, as any web host does. We do not use
    advertising trackers, and we do not sell or rent anyone's information — ever, to anyone.
  </p>

  <h2>Who can see it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Coaches and program leadership</strong>, to run the program and respond to
      emergencies.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Service providers</strong> that operate parts of the program on our behalf — our
      e-signature platform, payment processor, and email and messaging providers — which may use the
      information only to provide those services to us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><em>FIRST</em> and event hosts</strong>, where their own registration requires it.
      <em>FIRST</em> collects consent directly from families through its own system; that collection
      is governed by <em>FIRST</em>'s privacy policy, not this one.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Medical personnel</strong>, in an emergency.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Anyone we are legally required to disclose to.</strong>
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not share participant information with sponsors or donors. Aggregate figures we publish —
    such as the number of students in a season — never identify anyone.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Signed agreements are retained as long as needed to establish that consent was given, which may
    extend past the season. Contact and emergency information is retained for the season and while a
    student remains in the program. Working copies made for team operations, such as an exported
    contact list, are deleted once they have served their purpose.
  </p>
  <p>
    When a student leaves the program, we remove them from active rosters and messaging channels.
    Ask us and we will delete what we are not required to keep.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Media:</strong> you may decline media use at registration, and change your mind later
      by writing to us. We cannot recall material already published, and we cannot control
      recordings made by <em>FIRST</em>, event hosts, other teams, news media, or spectators at
      public events.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Access and correction:</strong> ask us what we hold about your family and we will tell
      you, and correct anything wrong.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Deletion:</strong> ask and we will delete what we are not required to retain.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Optional fields are genuinely optional.</strong> Leaving them blank does not affect a
      student's participation.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we protect it</h2>
  <p>
    Registration data lives with the e-signature platform that holds the signed agreements, rather
    than being copied across several systems. Access is limited to coaches and program leadership
    who need it. Exported copies are generated locally when needed for team operations and deleted
    afterward. We do not store participant information on this website or in our public source code.
  </p>
  <p>
    No system is perfectly secure, and we will not claim otherwise. If a breach affects your family's
    information, we will tell you.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions or concerns</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:info@stemplusc.org">info@stemplusc.org</a>. If something here concerns you,
    raise it — we would rather adjust what we collect than have a family uncomfortable with it.
  </p>
  <p>
    This notice sits alongside the
    <a href="/policies/team-agreement">Student &amp; Family Team Agreement</a> and the
    <a href="/policies/consent-release">Consent, Assumption of Risk, Release &amp; Emergency
    Authorization</a>. Where the consent agreement addresses the same subject, it governs.
  </p>
</PolicyLayout>
